(* README *)

1 - Summary
    -------

    L001 proves a local diagonal obstruction over M001's closed implication and
    falsity syntax. Its generic acceptance predicate

      C : Formula -> Prop

    has only the properties explicitly supplied to each theorem.

    The proof has two independent inputs:

      diagonal:     B ~=_C not B
      local branch: C B \/ C (not B)

    Modus ponens turns these into `C Bot`; consistency then yields `False`.
    A goal-restricted evaluation premise can produce the diagonal, but no
    universal evaluation frame is part of L001.

    Derived public theorems expose the same argument more precisely. They
    allow an arbitrary goal `G`, require only the fixed-point direction used
    by the selected branch, isolate the three local detachment instances, and
    show that consistency excludes both sides at a negation fixed point.
    These strengthenings do not add clauses to the six-contract aggregate.


2 - Reading Contract
    ----------------

    L001 is parametric in `C : Formula -> Prop`. The name "closure" does not
    silently supply modus ponens, consistency, excluded middle, reflection,
    proof search, decidability, or a semantic interpretation. Every property
    used by a theorem appears as an explicit premise.

    `ClosureSignedClassification C` certifies one of two internal branches:

      true  -> C A
      false -> C (formula_negation A)

    `ClosureMembershipDecision C` instead decides membership in `C`. Turning
    non-membership into `C (formula_negation A)` requires the separate premise
    `ClosureRefutationComplete C`.

    Negative-only refutation has no condition on a false verdict, so the
    always-false function inhabits it for every `C`.

    `ClosureEvaluationFrameForGoal C Code ev G` is goal-restricted. It
    represents only the anti-diagonal behavior needed for the selected `G`;
    it is not a universal evaluation structure. L001 does not construct such
    a frame for M001 checked derivability.


3 - State
    -----

                      ┌──────────────────────────────────┐
                      │                x                 │
                      │   └─┴─┴─┴─┴─┴─┴─┴─┴─┴─┘ 7 / 10   │
                      └──────────────────────────────────┘

    Evaluation: 7, Serviceable. Mechanized, documented, and reduced to six
    explicit contracts. The proof is constructive and assumption-local. Not
    peer reviewed.


4 - Intuition
    ---------

    A negation fixed point is not a syntactic equality. It is the pair of
    accepted implications

      C (Imp B (formula_negation B))
      C (Imp (formula_negation B) B).

    If the regulator also supplies the local branch

      C B \/ C (formula_negation B),

    then either branch can be detached through the corresponding fixed-point
    direction. The result is acceptance of both `B` and its negation, followed
    by acceptance of `Bot`.

      fixed-point implications + one local branch
                         │
                         ▼
              local_branch_collapse
                         │
                         ▼
                       C Bot

    Consistency excludes that conclusion, so both local branches are absent
    at the fixed point. Global closure-level excluded middle is obstructed
    because it would supply this one forbidden instance.

    The branchwise theorem is sharper: for an arbitrary goal `G`, it names
    only the three detachment instances needed by the proof and uses only the
    fixed-point direction aligned with the selected branch.

    Signed classification supplies the forbidden local branch directly.
    Membership decision supplies it only with refutation completeness.
    Negative-only refutation supplies no such branch and is always inhabited.


